// a capacity whose byte size does not fit a usize used to wrap to a tiny allocation, with the huge
// capacity recorded anyway. now the allocation is refused. read back on purpose: an array that is
// written and dropped is one the optimizer may remove whole, and the stop has to hold for that one too

array<int64> $a = [];
$a->reserve(2305843009213693953);
$a[] = 1;
echo $a[0];
echo 'unreachable';
